# Glassdoor

> Glassdoor is a jobs and career community where people find job listings, company reviews, salary data, and career advice drawn from insights shared by real employees.

## About

- [Glassdoor](https://www.glassdoor.com/index.htm): Search jobs and explore company reviews, salaries, and interview insights.
- [About Glassdoor](https://www.glassdoor.com/about/): Company overview, mission, leadership, and press resources.
- [Trust & Transparency](https://www.glassdoor.com/about/trust/): How Glassdoor moderates reviews, handles content removal requests, and protects reviewer anonymity.

## Blog: Career Advice Hub

- [Glassdoor Blog](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/): Career advice covering job search, interviews, pay, and workplace trends from Glassdoor's team of career experts.

## Blog: Economic Research & Data

- [Glassdoor Worklife Trends 2026: Midyear Check-In](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/worklife-trends-2026-midyear-check-in/): Glassdoor Economic Research revisits its 2026 workplace predictions with fresh review, ratings, and interview data on leadership trust, layoffs, return-to-office, AI sentiment, and job offers.
- [Glassdoor Employee Confidence Index: Rebound From Record Low](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/glassdoor-employee-confidence-index-june-2026/): Glassdoor's monthly proprietary index tracking U.S. employee sentiment on their employer's six-month outlook, broken out by industry and seniority.
- [June Jobs Report: No Fireworks](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/bls-jobs-report-june-2026/): Glassdoor's Chief Economist analyzes the latest BLS jobs report and what it means for job seekers, employers, and investors.
- [The Layoff Recovery Roadmap: What Job Seekers Say Helps the Most](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/layoff-recovery-roadmap-job-search/): Glassdoor Community poll data and Economic Research findings on how long layoff anxiety lingers and what actually helps workers recover.
- [Conversation Starter: Does Money Buy Loyalty?](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/conversation-starter-does-money-buy-loyalty/): A Glassdoor data scientist compares self-reported pay to Glassdoor's salary estimates to show how compensation gaps affect employee satisfaction and job searching.
- [Conversation Starter: How Landing an Interview Changes With Experience](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/conversation-starter-landing-interviews-experience/): Glassdoor interview data shows how online applications, recruiter outreach, and referrals vary in effectiveness by years of experience.
- [Economic Research](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/category/research/): Ongoing labor market analysis and workplace research from Glassdoor's economists and data scientists.

## Blog: Pay and Salary

- [Pay and Salary Guides](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/guide/category/pay-salary/): Guides on salaries, raises, negotiation, and pay transparency.
- [Beyond the Gap 2026: Redefining Career Success & Compensation for Women](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/guide/beyond-the-gap-women-compensation-report/): Glassdoor research on how the gender pay gap widens over a woman's career, plus Community-sourced strategies for negotiating beyond salary.

## Blog: Job Search and Hiring

- [Job Search Guides](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/guide/category/job-search/): Guides on finding, applying for, and landing a job.

## Best Places to Work and Research

- [Glassdoor Awards](https://www.glassdoor.com/Award/index.htm): Glassdoor's Employees' Choice Awards, including Best Places to Work.
- [Best Places to Work 2026](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/glassdoor-announces-best-places-to-work-2026/): Announcement of the Best Places to Work 2026 winners.
- [Glassdoor's Best Places to Work 2026: Companies Hiring Now](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/best-places-to-work-revealed/): The 2026 Best Places to Work winners that are actively hiring, with employee insights.
- [Best Places to Work Awards Criteria](https://www.glassdoor.com/blog/glassdoor-announces-awards-criteria-for-the-best-places-to-work/): How companies are evaluated for the Best Places to Work awards.

